{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310708,"nonce":"qKFWlRYL7rts7tGw8hgUg7ZTdN8=","title":"FIXED 2026-09-19 — a user/stdlib static call bound to ANOTHER class's runtime row by bare method name (F1.fromFloat -\u003e ...","message":"Three defects found while making `Int64.parseString`/`fromFloat` and `import haxe.Int64.*` work (TestInt64 COMPILE_FAIL -\u003e runs, 12 FAILCHECK left). git-bug c48823d, 590ec29, 80194a2.\n\n1. **By-name static scans in MIR.** Four call probes fell back to `find_static_method_by_name_and_params` / `find_unique_static_by_name_and_params` / `find_unique_by_method` when the class-qualified mapping lookup missed. `rayzor.SIMD4i32.fromFloat` is the only static `fromFloat` row, so `F1.fromFloat`, `haxe.Int64.fromFloat` and wildcard `fromFloat(..)` ALL became `SIMD4i32_from_float` (LLVM: \"Unsupported cast F64 -\u003e Vector\"). Rule now: a symbol WITH a qualified name is looked up under that owner only; the Field-callee path also asks `StaticSigIndex::indexed_declares_static` (read-only, never parses). The instance-path `find_unique_by_method` in stdlib_runtime.rs is STILL a by-name scan.\n\n2. **Expected-abstract redirect ate locals.** `ast_lowering/expr/mod.rs` redirects a bare identifier to a static of the *expected* abstract type (enum-abstract constants), and the expected type falls back to the function's declared RETURN type. So in any `:Int64` function, a local `neg`/`add`/`make` became `Int64.neg`. Symptom: ternary lowered to nothing, `rest` unbound, tail `unreachable`, LLVM folded the body into the guard's throw (\"Number is NaN or Infinite\" for 3.0). Now locals/params shadow and only non-Function statics qualify.\n\n3. **Same-package forward reference.** `Int64Helper` inside haxe/Int64.hx (cycle: each imports the other) resolved to nothing and the abstract fallback made it `this.Int64Helper`. Now `same_package_type_placeholder` mints the import placeholder when `namespace_resolver.declared_kind(\"\u003cpkg\u003e.\u003cName\u003e\")` reads a declaration. Also: the multi-segment static path (`haxe.Int64.fromFloat`) accepted only `SymbolKind::Class` — abstracts went to the instance path.\n\n**Why:** \"the mapping has a row with this name\" is not \"this call is that row\". Every by-name scan is a latent wrong-binding; with 4 backends the symptom lands in whichever backend rejects the type mismatch.\n\n**How to apply:** `RAYZOR_LOWER_TRACE=1` (cached debug flag) prints `[lower-none] variable/unary/if/call ...` for every non-Void expression MIR produced no value for, and `[lower-call] lowered|consumed by \u003cprobe\u003e` — read it BEFORE guessing which probe or pass is at fault (I burned 4 builds on forward_ref.rs, which turned out unnecessary; `/tmp/probe/fwd.patch`). A single-file probe needs NO class path, but a multi-file probe needs a `rayzor.toml` with `class-paths = [\".\"]` next to it, else siblings silently do not load and the call binds by bare name to whatever exists. Fixtures DynamicDispatch/TemplateBasics FAIL under `check-regressions.py --llvm` at HEAD too (pre-existing; default tiered path is 25/25).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_static_calls_bound_by_bare_method_name` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}